Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure AS-map file loading and selected version

Preserve all four Info diagnostics and the original read/parse/startup
paths. ftell length remains a signed integer, not unsigned Bytes; the actual
AS-map uint256 version gets its own HASH key instead of BlockHash. Message
paths retain fs::quoted ampersand/quote escaping, while JSON stores raw paths.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0, exact reviewed calls and registry additions):
  /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/asmap-file-diagnostics.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/asmap224-apply.json --apply
  git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/util/asmap.cpp src/init.cpp src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp
  /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/n4-harness-intake/venv/bin/ruff format test/functional/feature_logging_asmap.py

Manual native test calls real DecodeAsmap for a missing file and invalid
one-byte map, checking unchanged empty results, signed length and original
strprintf path text. The isolated functional test loads the upstream59-byte
fixture through an ampersand/quote path and checks the known AS-map version
already asserted in feature_asmap.py, then flushes for typed JSON checks.

A first catalog input assumed init.cpp directly included logging.h; exact
support-anchor validation rejected it without writing sources. Re-derive
from the observed unique kernel/caches.h anchor; correction receipt retained.
This was a tool-input correction, not a product/test failure.

Validation at commit: event lint432 sites, Ruff and whitespace pass. Native
proof pending with the coherent registry batch; immutable native215 retained.
Tier: shared eCash; V2 inherits. No algorithm or network-policy changes.

Coordinator causal prerequisite repair (2026-10-20):
The shared AS-map logging change does not use pool types and must not include node/mining_pool.h before that native-only header exists. Keep the include with the actual native pool first consumer stable141. Exact final507 source tree remains unchanged; failed shared362 build and all ordered-tree/metadata proofs are preserved in final507-header-repair-delivery. No new purpose or compatibility shim; benchmarkworker owns incremental shared compilation.
